<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Santa River (Peru)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Santa River is a river of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> that rises at Lake Conococha in the Andes, flows north through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/callejon-de-huaylas">Callejón de Huaylas</a> and then turns west to reach the Pacific near Chimbote. Its valley was settled by the Recuay culture and other Andean societies, and today it supplies irrigation and hydroelectric power.</p></div>
